From d0c5604382c6b0350887b58b56c2ee101e6b36bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:02:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Spike: supply the deep-crown integral's rows at an
 active scalar

The crown integral is one tape statement with its rows taken in double: each
light read is linear in its span's coefficients, and the leaf rate's partials
are written once. The value is the recorded loop's bit for bit; a read outside
the spline's interior falls back to the recorded loop. A sweep walks one
statement and a row per input rather than 43 statements and 232 operations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFsPxk1yy62LrcCbtZUVeB
